From: Joel Winarske <joel.winarske@linux.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Expose Firestore sum and average on desktop

Query::Count() is the only aggregation the C++ SDK offers, so a caller who
wants a sum has to download every document and add them up.

The vendored Firestore core already does the rest. api::Query::Aggregate takes
a vector of model::AggregateField, model::AggregateField::OpKind is
{Sum, Avg, Count}, and FirestoreClient::RunAggregateQuery and the serializer
carry it to the wire. Nothing calls any of it: QueryInternal::Count() reaches
for query_.Count(), and query_.Aggregate() has no caller at all.

So this is exposure, not implementation, and it does not touch the vendored
library.

Query::Sum and Query::Average take a dot-separated field path and return an
AggregateQuery. AggregateQuerySnapshot::value() answers for all three kinds --
the count for a count, the computed number otherwise -- so there is no way to
ask a snapshot for a result it does not hold. count() on a sum returns zero
rather than the sum truncated to an integer, which would look like a count
that worked.

A sum comes back as an integer when every input was an integer and as a double
otherwise, so both proto types are read. A missing alias means the aggregation
had nothing to work on and reads as zero.

Desktop only, guarded by FIREBASE_PLATFORM_DESKTOP: the Android and iOS
implementations have their own aggregate paths and this does not touch them.

Upstream has firebase/firebase-cpp-sdk#1703 asking for SUM and #1705 as a WIP
PR. That PR does not implement the desktop path -- its QueryInternal::Aggregate
is a TODO that falls off the end of a non-void function -- and it has been
conflicting since April 2025. AVERAGE has neither an issue nor a PR.

diff --git a/firestore/src/common/aggregate_query_snapshot.cc b/firestore/src/common/aggregate_query_snapshot.cc
index 0c8f9b1..18fca5e 100644
Upstream-Status: Pending

Carried by firebase_ffi, where the set is maintained:
https://github.com/jwinarske/firebase_ffi/tree/main/packages/firebase_ffi/patches/firebase-cpp-sdk
